      </language>
      <purpose>To record a narrative description and clinical interpretation of the findings observed during the physical examination of an area of oedema at an identified body site.</purpose>
      <use>Use to record a narrative description and clinical interpretation of the findings observed during the physical examination of an area of oedema at an identified body site.&#xD;
&#xD;
This archetype has been specifically designed to be used in the 'Examination detail' SLOT within the CLUSTER.limb or CLUSTER.back archetypes which provide the context for the structure or system that is being examined. This archetype can also be used within other ENTRY or CLUSTER archetypes that provide relevant system or structure context, where clinically appropriate.&#xD;
&#xD;
The CLUSTER.exclusion_exam archetype can be nested within the 'Examination not done' SLOT to optionally record explicit details about the examination not being performed.&#xD;
&#xD;
Use to incorporate the narrative descriptions of clinical findings within existing or legacy clinical systems into an archetyped format, using the 'Clinical Description' data element.</use>
      <misuse>Not to be used for recording the clinical history - use specific OBSERVATION and CLUSTER archetypes. For example OBSERVATION.story and CLUSTER.symptom_sign.</misuse>
      <copyright>© openEHR Foundation</copyright>
    </details>
